 "notes": "Spread: annotations on left page (p. 106, headed HOW TO TRADE IN STOCKS), ledger grid on right page (p. 107, headed CHART THREE with Livermore Market-Key crest). Year header \"1938\" appears once above DATE; no new year appears mid-chart. Date rows run JUNE17 through 29 (July 29); rows JUNE17, SAT.18, 27, 28, 5, 6, 8, SAT.9, 13, 14, 15, SAT16, 18, 20, 21, 22, SAT23, 26, 27, 28, 29 have no handwritten entries and are omitted. July 4 (Monday, holiday) has no row - the sequence jumps from SAT.2 to 5. KP = US + BS checksum verified and consistent on every row where all three instruments have entries (June 20, 21, 22, 23, 24, 25, 29, 30, July 2, 11, 19); on single/double-entry days (July 1, 7, 12, 25) KP equals the new US price plus the prior BS price, also consistent. Header carried-forward entries occupy four lines above the DATE row: line 1 = DT pivots 38/40/78 (red, double black underline); line 2 = NR pivots 49/52/101 (blue, double black underline); line 3 = 39 1/4 (US NRC), 39 3/4 (BS DT, red, double underlined), 79 (KP NRC), where 39 1/4 + 39 3/4 = 79; line 4 = 46 1/2 in BS SR (blue). All drawn underlines within the dated rows are single red lines hugging the number width, marking the extreme price before a column change (BS topped July 2 at 62 1/2 and again July 19 at 63 1/8; US/KP topped July 7 at 61 3/4 / 124 1/4 and July 25 at 63 1/4 / 126 3/8; reaction lows underlined July 11 for BS 56 3/4 and July 12 for US 55 1/2 / KP 112 1/4). Ink colors matched expected column coding throughout (UT black, DT red, others blue pencil); no contradictions found, no illegible cells.",
